{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>How many are the days of the years of your life.</b> The plain sense: because he saw him very old and the hair of his head and his beard white from much old age, he asked thus. And he answered him: ״The days of my sojournings are thirty and a hundred years; few and evil.״ That is, my years are few, but because of the evil that was upon me, old age rushed upon me. Midrash: At the moment Jacob said ״few and evil,״ the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: I rescued you from Esau and from Laban, and I returned Dinah to you, also Joseph — and you complain about your life, that they are few and evil? By your life, the number of words that there are from ״ויאמר״ until ״בימי מגורי״ — thus shall be subtracted from your years, that you shall not live as long as the life of Isaac your father. And they are 33 words, and by this number they were subtracted from his life, for Isaac lived 180 years and Jacob lived only 147."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:14.224792775Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}